<section class="source-band" aria-labelledby="retrieval-fault-heading">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">What happened</p>
      <h2 id="retrieval-fault-heading">A missing record is still a record of something.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        The address you followed does not resolve to a catalogued object,
        dossier, or transmission. That usually means one of three things: the
        record was renamed as the native taxonomy settled, the link was
        transcribed with a missing segment, or the item has not yet been
        accessioned into the public archive.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing has been deleted to produce this page. Sources are preserved
        even when their public route changes, so the material you were looking
        for may simply be filed under a newer address.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

